    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d691">

                <pb facs="1071" n="1055" sameAs="frus:frus1949v06/pg1055"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">501.BB Palestine/5–2549: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The United States Representative at the United
                        Nations</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Austin</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">secret</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">New York</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1949-05-25T19:05:00-04:00">May 25, 1949—7:05
                            p. m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>644. Bunche and Riley were both of opinion last evening that disclosure of
                    Israeli territorial aspirations to PCC will result in breakdown of
                    Israeli-Syrian armistice negotiations. They also agree that <pb facs="1072"
                        n="1056" xml:id="pg1056"/> this disclosure will probably wreck PCC talks and
                    might also threaten armistice agreements.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Austin</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
